  "final_answer": "All four deliverables are written to `/app` and cross-check out:\n\n- **`composite_request_audit.csv`** \u2014 37 rows, columns `request_id,finding`; one row per finding (clean requests \u2192 `none`). Withdrawn REQ-13/16/26/31 excluded.\n- **`account_summary.csv`** \u2014 8 rows, columns `account_id,account_type,request_count,flagged_requests,escalation`.\n- **`composite_request_memo.md`** \u2014 standalone memo (audit date, out-of-scope requests, every finding with its deciding record, the personal-use-allowance clears, master-agreement standing, and the \u00a78 decisions against the 50% batch share).\n- **`results.json`** \u2014 the eleven \u00a79 figures, each a single number.\n\n**Batch figures:** 28 audited / 8 accounts / 14 flagged / 14 compliant / 23 findings \u2014 character 6, background 5, consent 3, commercial 6, disclosure 3 / 4 escalated (ACC-02, ACC-03, ACC-07, ACC-08).\n\nKey judgement calls, per INT-09: supersession narrows terms (REQ-05 hits LIC-109's 20% cap, not LIC-103's 35%; REQ-28/REQ-18 use LIC-110's `print_for_sale` scope, not LIC-105's `all`); the two lapsed agreements (ACC-04, ACC-08) cover nothing; ACC-05 is active-but-narrow (clears `print_for_sale`, not `social_public`); `personal_only` clears \u00a73 entirely (REQ-01/22/32 would otherwise breach on prominence); and \u00a78 escalates ACC-02/03 on the three-findings limb and ACC-07/08 on the share limb (66.7% > 50.0%).",
